---
title: Pleiades Work-Precision Diagrams
author: Chris Rackauckas
---

```julia
using OrdinaryDiffEq, ODEInterfaceDiffEq, LSODA, Sundials, DiffEqDevTools, IRKGaussLegendre
using OrdinaryDiffEqAdamsBashforthMoulton, OrdinaryDiffEqExtrapolation, OrdinaryDiffEqHighOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqLowOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqSDC
using SciMLLogging

f = (du, u, p, t) -> begin
    @inbounds begin
        x = view(u, 1:7)   # x
        y = view(u, 8:14)  # y
        v = view(u, 15:21) # x′
        w = view(u, 22:28) # y′
        du[1:7] .= v
        du[8:14] .= w
        for i in 15:28
            du[i] = zero(u[1])
        end
        for i in 1:7, j in 1:7

            if i != j
                r = ((x[i]-x[j])^2 + (y[i] - y[j])^2)^(3/2)
                du[14 + i] += j*(x[j] - x[i])/r
                du[21 + i] += j*(y[j] - y[i])/r
            end
        end
    end
end

prob = ODEProblem{true, SciMLBase.FullSpecialize}(f,
    [3.0, 3.0, -1.0, -3.0, 2.0, -2.0, 2.0, 3.0, -3.0, 2.0, 0, 0,
        -4.0, 4.0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1.75, -1.5, 0, 0, 0, -1.25, 1, 0, 0],
    (0.0, 3.0))

abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (6:9)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (3:6);

using Plots;
gr()
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "..", "workprecision_table.jl"))

const PLEIADES_ERROR_FLOOR = 1.0e-9
const PLEIADES_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS = [:irkgl, :implicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS = [:sundials, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:sundials, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_LSODA_TAGS = [:lsoda, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const PLEIADES_SDC_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :sdc, :nonstiff]
```

Each sweep requests only the error metrics needed for its measurement with
`error_estimates` and attaches solver metadata tags to the results. The table
with each work-precision figure reports the best endpoint error, that point's
timing, right-hand-side calls, accepted steps, and a computed refinement rate
when the tolerance grid resolves one. Rate calculations exclude errors at or
below `1e-9`, a conservative bound above the measured final-point gap between
the reference and a tighter solve; an em dash means that the rate or counter is
unavailable or unresolved. The plotted reference trajectory retains dense output
because the figure and interpolation-error references consume it; the endpoint
reference uses endpoint-only output.

```julia
sol = solve(prob, Vern8(), abstol = 1/10^12, reltol = 1/10^10, maxiters = 1000000)
sol_endpoint = solve(prob, Vern8(), abstol = 1/10^12, reltol = 1/10^10, maxiters = 1000000,
    save_everystep = false, dense = false)
test_sol_dense = sol
test_sol = sol_endpoint
plot(sol)
```

## Low Order

ODE.jl is not part of this benchmark's environment; its setups are left commented out for reference.

```julia
#setups = [Dict(:alg=>ode45())]
#wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob,abstols,reltols,setups;appxsol=test_sol,save_everystep=false,numruns=100,maxiters=10000)
#plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>dopri5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)]
low_order_setups = setups
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol,
    error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100, maxiters = 10000)
low_order_wp = wp
print_work_table(wp, PLEIADES_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

### Interpolation

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol_dense, error_estimates = [:final, :l2, :L2], verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100,
    maxiters = 10000, error_estimate = :L2, dense_errors = true)
print_work_table(wp, PLEIADES_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

