## Comparison with Non-RK methods

Now let's test Tsit5 and Vern9 against parallel extrapolation methods and an
Adams-Bashforth-Moulton:

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>PLEIADES_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>VCABM(), :tags=>PLEIADES_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>AitkenNeville(min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)]
solnames = ["Tsit5", "Vern9", "VCABM", "IRKGL16", "IRKGL16 SIMD",
    "AitkenNeville", "Midpoint Deuflhard", "Midpoint Hairer Wanner"]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final], names = solnames,
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
print_work_table(wp, PLEIADES_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 9, threading = false), :tags=>PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = false), :tags=>PLEIADES_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
